Backport: Revert "player: do not exit when a seek gets queued"
Origin: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/d59f4fd3ec141693da4f7f6677aa729e1bb92f4d
Upstream-Date: 2024-05-16
Applied-to: mpv 0.38.0
Modified-by: ChengYingPlayer maintainers, 2026-09-21

This is the complete upstream fix for mpv issue #13778. Queueing a seek must
not clear the end-of-file stop reason before the seek is actually executed.
An on_unload hook can queue a refresh seek when changing video-rotate; clearing
the stop reason there violates play_current_file's teardown assertion.
The matching play-direction workaround is removed as in the upstream commit.
Only hunk line numbers are adapted to the 0.38.0 release tarball. The existing
assertion and public libmpv ABI version remain unchanged.

